 ### Parameters and Edge Cases
-- **Parameters:** The method generates exactly 3 levels (mip 0, 1, 2). The downsampling factor is always 2 per dimension.
-- **Edge Cases:** If any dimension of the input is less than 2, the corresponding mip level dimension becomes 0, and the loop for that level will not execute. The bitwise OR operation ensures that shadow presence is never lost, but detail is reduced.
-- **Pitfalls:** Precision issues are minimal as only integer division and bitwise operations are used. Boundary conditions are handled by the integer division which effectively maps 4 parent voxels to 1 child voxel.
-
-### Subtopics
-- **Bitwise OR Accumulation:** A downsampling technique where child values are the logical OR of parent values. It is chosen when binary presence/absence (like shadowing) must be preserved across resolutions. It differs from averaging (used in density mips) by being non-destructive to presence. [Bitwise OR Mipmap Accumulation](2602-mipmap-generation.md#subtopics)
-- **3D Texture Mipmapping:** The process of generating lower-resolution versions of a 3D texture. This method is specific to shadow volumes, whereas general 3D mipmapping might use different filtering. [GPU 3D Mip Chain Generation](5067-gpu-3d-mip-chain-generation.md)
